    {
      "name": "resolution_time_hours",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.35,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Resolution time is a highly useful axis for incident analysis (SLA, bottlenecks). But the values are not grounded: closed_at equals sys_updated_on in every sample, so the true resolution span isn't derivable from the shown fields, and produced values (286.8, 348.6, 418.8) are inconsistent with the identical timestamps. A negative value (-4.3) is impossible and confirms fabricated/erroneous computation."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_critical",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.45,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "rationale": "A criticality flag could support prioritization analysis, but it is largely redundant with the existing 'priority' column and is a bare binary flag, limiting new leverage. It is plausibly derivable from priority; the samples show all 0 which is consistent but not strongly verifiable from the shown text.",
      "hallucination_observed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "domain_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "rationale": "Categorizing tickets into Infrastructure/Database/Software gives a genuine grouping axis for analysis and is somewhat distinct from the raw 'category'. Values are well-grounded readings of short_description (database->Database, VPN/intranet/internet->Infrastructure, software update->Software).",
      "hallucination_observed": false
    },
    {
      "name": "recurrence_indicator",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.4,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Recurrence/repeat-issue detection is a reasonable analytical axis. But the integer values (0,1,2,3) are not clearly derivable from single-row text; 'frequent disconnection' got 1 while a plain 'software update issue' also got 0 and 'database' got 1, showing no coherent, text-supported mapping. The values appear asserted rather than grounded."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
  "source_groundedness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "The added columns offer genuinely useful new axes (domain categorization, resolution time, criticality, recurrence) beyond the raw fields, so analytical usefulness is moderate-to-high overall. However groundedness is dragged down by resolution_time_hours (impossible negatives and values inconsistent with identical closed_at/sys_updated_on timestamps) and recurrence_indicator (integer counts with no coherent basis in the single-row source text). domain_type is well-grounded and is_critical is plausible though redundant with priority."
}

